To give players more control over the risks they face while moving through the location and reduce their dependence on random factors, the following changes have been made:
- Rogues have moved from the water treatment plant to the mountain chalets;
- There are no longer any stationary weapons at the water treatment plant;
- The open areas along the main road have been reworked to provide more cover and additional routes;
- All landmines have been removed from the water treatment plant;
- A transition point to Icebreaker has been added to the location. The hovercraft stays at the pier near the water cottages;
- A temporary task chain focused on the shifting faction balance on Lighthouse has been added;
- Loot distribution has been reworked. Rogue stashes containing their abandoned gear have been added throughout the location;
- The BTR now patrols the location. Its route has several variants and covers the entire location, including the approach to the bridge leading to the peninsula and the water treatment plant;
- Underground passages have been added in the mountains, shortening the route to the extracts in the southern part of the location;
- The Marked Room has been moved from Lightkeeper's peninsula;
- The locations of key points required for main story tasks have been changed:
  - Prapor's camp has been relocated.

The task chain that unlocks access to Lightkeeper, as well as the requirements to start it, have been completely reworked. The chain is now more focused on testing the player's skills rather than repetitive tasks of the same type.

To receive the first task in the "To the Light" chain, you must:
- Gain access to Lighthouse through the "Tour" storyline;
- Have Loyalty Level 3 with all traders except Fence and Ref;
- Have at least 2.0 reputation with Fence;
- Ask Mechanic about the possibility of working with Lightkeeper.

- Icebreaker can now be accessed from Shoreline and Lighthouse;
- Icebreaker no longer requires a payment in roubles, but does require a one-time use "Sudak-tudak" marine repair kit.
This item can be obtained by completing Ragman's "Pay the Fare!" task. After completing it, you'll gain access to a special type of operational task that rewards more "Sudak-tudak" repair kits.

- Added an indicator for tasks for which an item can currently be handed over;
- Added the ability to view the profile of and report a PMC or player Scav from the list of killed players after a raid;
- Increased the area that must be hit to shoot off the lock on a container or door;
- Added the "Can't Drink Away Skill" task, which rewards the Loui Peeton wallet. The task becomes available after completing "Is This a Reference?";
- Added an Icebreaker Model Kit item to the rewards for the "Part of the Ship, Part of the Crew" achievement, along with a crafting recipe using this item;
- Adjusted the attitude of Rogues toward USEC characters.

- Adjusted the XP multiplier awarded for transitions. It will now increase more gradually, starting at a lower value than before for 1-2 transitions and reaching the previous values at 16 or more transitions;
- Reduced the XP gained for eliminating Wedge, his squad, and Black Division operatives on Icebreaker;
- Reduced the XP gained for eliminating Shadow of Tagilla, Vengeful Killa, and Scavs in The Labyrinth;
- Reduced the purchase price of euros and dollars from traders;
- Changed the sale price of the HK MP5 at Mechanic and Peacekeeper Loyalty Level 2;
- Removed armor from the following face masks:
  - Glorious E mask;
  - Shattered mask;
  - DevTac Samurai Menpo Mask;
  - DevTac Samurai Menpo Mask (White);
  - Death Shadow mask;
  - Death Shadow mask (Gray).

- Fixed an issue that caused saved weapon presets to disappear after a raid;
- Fixed issues with empty keybind entries in the controls settings for some players;
- Fixed an issue where, with the Fresh Wound effect active and the Dr. Jekyll modifier selected, bleeding effects would open too frequently;
- Excessive shading in the visuals at the Labs location and certain other locations has been fixed;
- Fixed part of the environment disappearing in Spectator Mode on Reserve;
- Fixed incorrect display of body-part health in Spectator Mode in some cases;
- Fixed known issues that could cause padlocked doors to remain impassable even after the lock had been shot off;
- Fixed hit registration issues when firing bolt-action rifles immediately after mounting them on a bipod;
- Fixed incorrect display of the character's wrist when inspecting certain weapons;
- Fixed issues with reloading weapons using magazines from pockets when the player had an unsearched rig equipped;
- Fixed an issue where the Strength and Endurance skills would not level up during the first raid after training in the Hideout gym;
- Fixed an issue where some items could continue to be marked as available for task handover even after they were no longer required;
- Fixed an issue where regular Scavs would become hostile toward a player Scav who had damaged a Black Division operative;
- Fixed bot reactions to gas grenade throws;
- Made various UI/UX fixes and improvements to the character selection and gesture screens, magazine preset loading, and the main menu while in a raid;
- Fixed some issues that could cause the game to crash while loading into a raid;
- Fixed various culling and environment issues across multiple locations;
- Fixed an issue where creating a character would clear the list of favorite crafting recipes in other modes;
- Fixed an issue that prevented some posters from being placed in the Hideout;
- Removed ammunition from the magazines of some weapon presets in trader inventories;
- Added the missing weapon attachments from Patch 1.1.0.0 to Peacekeeper's stock;
- Fixed the incorrect weapon presets for Sanitar, Killa, and Kaban's guards.

- Fixed certain keybinds being displayed as NONE in the control settings, which resulted in the inability to use such hotkeys;
- Fixed the issue where PMC fatigue effects were triggered when stamina was at full capacity in some cases;
- Fixed a darkening effect in the Lab location if the player had previously been in a raid in an open location;
- Fixed an issue with freezing on a blank screen after leaving a raid in some cases;
- Fixed some issues with the culling system in the Ground Zero location;
- Fixed incorrect weapon grip animations in some cases;
- Fixed an issue that made it impossible to ADS in the Hideout's Shooting Range after visiting a trader;
- Fixed the behavior of the post-death ragdoll in some cases.

- Fixed a number of culling issues at the Customs location;
- Fixed an error that occurred during the loading in raid when playing with a seasonal character and in the PvE ZONE in certain cases;
- Fixed incorrect input handling when using hotkeys assigned to the arrow keys.
- The number of documents has been increased to 14 on all locations. On Factory location, the number of documents has been increased to 10;
- The daily limit on the transfer of documents has been increased for each mode:
  - PVP Season: from 25 to 30 documents;
  - PVP: from 15 to 20 documents;
  - PVE ZONE: from 10 to 15 documents.
- Please note that the count towards the available document transfer limit begins as soon as at least one document has been taken out of the raid.

- Fixed an issue that prevented the door in A.P.'s corporate apartment on Streets of Tarkov from opening after using the keycard;
- Fixed an issue that caused the “Juice Time” and “Sailor’s Nostalgia” modifiers to activate when the player canceled an item’s use before the animation started;
- Fixed an issue where attachment icons were displayed incorrectly in the missing parts window when building a weapon;
- Fixed several issues with environment display in spectator mode;
- Fixed the incorrect QBZ-191 grip when used with foregrips.

- Fixed an issue that made it impossible to enter Lightkeeper's chamber.
- Fixed an issue where players with the "Well that hurt!" or "Diet" modifiers would encounter error 228 when using medkits or provisions with partially depleted resource;
- Made balancing changes to the stats of some stocks;
- Made balancing changes to the stats of 5.8x42 ammunition.

- Fixed an issue where players were unable to receive side tasks from Prapor after visiting him for the first time;
- Minor balancing changes to side tasks;
- Fixed an issue where players were receiving Kord Breach season achievements in PvP mode.

- Fixed several issues causing an error to appear immediately after launching the game client;
- Fixed an issue where loyalty levels with traders were displayed incorrectly, as well as issues with accepting side tasks in some cases;
- Fixed an issue where Q and E key inputs were not processed correctly in some cases;
- Fixed a problem with parts of the environment disappearing in spectator mode in some cases;
- Fixed the streamer mode not being active on the character selection screen;
- Fixed the constant display of the exit timer in spectator mode in some cases;
- Improved weapon animations when bumping into surfaces in third person;
- Fixed the display of Hideout modules' highlights in first person mode;
- Fixed incorrect first person hand animations when opening a door in spectator mode;
- Fixed the display of seasonal achievement icons when viewing a friend's profile;
- Fixed an issue where rewards from previous Twitch Drops campaigns were not available to seasonal characters;
- Fixed a weapon and ammo mismatch in some containers from support messages;
- Various localization fixes;
- Fixed an issue causing incorrect reputation values to be earned from side tasks.

- Apply only to Seasonal Characters;
- Are enabled for all players participating in the season;
- Cannot be changed, disabled, or selected individually.

Each new season will feature a different set of Global modifiers, creating a fresh gameplay experience and new progression challenges.

In the future, we are also considering community voting that would allow players to influence the selection of Global modifiers for upcoming seasons.

A complete list of active Global modifiers is displayed during Seasonal Character creation.

- Increased the trader prices by an average of 25%;
- Reduced the price traders pay for items sold by players by an average of 20%;
- Increased the Flea Market fee from 3% to 5%.

- Removed the required trader sales volume from Loyalty Level requirements;
- Rebalanced the reputation requirements for all Loyalty Levels of the following traders: Prapor, Therapist, Fence, Skier, Peacekeeper, Mechanic, Ragman, and Jaeger;
- Reputation rewards from side tasks have also been adjusted;
  - Reputation values for existing PvP Zone and PvE Zone characters have been recalculated based on the new requirements.
  - Rebalanced the character level requirements for all Loyalty Levels of the listed traders.

- Several popular ammunition types and magazines previously sold at Trader Loyalty Levels 2 and 3 have been moved down by one Loyalty Level, making them available earlier.
- Reduced the price of the following ammunition:
  - 5.45x39mm FMJ
  - 5.56x45mm FMJ
  - 7.62x39mm FMJ
  - 9x19mm Green Tracer
  - .45 ACP Lasermatch FMJ
- Added new weapon presets to Trader Loyalty Level 1 for several traders;
- Many trader offers previously locked behind task completion are now available immediately upon reaching the required Trader Loyalty Level;
- Some trader offers previously unlocked through tasks have been moved to different task rewards;
  - Players who had previously unlocked these offers will lose access to them until they complete the new required task;
- Removed the outdated trade offers that could still appear in Flea Market tooltips;
- Ref's inventory now primarily features armor vests and plate carriers without armor plates installed, and their prices have been reduced accordingly;
- Significantly reworked weapon mod trader offers, including which traders and Loyalty Levels unlock them, as well as their prices and purchase limits.

- Simplified the construction requirements for some Level 1-3 Hideout zones;
  - In both PvP Zone and PvE Zone, the Found in Raid requirement has been removed from some construction materials;
- Reduced construction times for certain Hideout zones;
- The Workbench is no longer required to access the Weapon Build system. Weapon builds are now available from the start of the game;
- Added money requirements to the construction of many Hideout areas;
- Some crafting recipes previously unlocked through tasks have been moved to different task rewards;
  - Players who had previously unlocked these recipes will lose access to them until they complete the new required task.

- Applies only to PvP Zone and PvE Zone, as insurance is disabled in PvP Season:
  - Added a new insurance option from Jaeger. It offers the fastest return time but is also the most expensive. However, Jaeger doesn't like to wait, so insurance return messages expire much sooner;
  - Insurance returns from Prapor and Therapist are now much faster, though their insurance services have become slightly more expensive. Insurance return messages are also stored for longer;
  - Higher Trader Loyalty Levels now provide a small discount on insurance.

- Tactical clothing purchased from Ragman is now permanently unlocked on your account. You no longer need to repurchase it after resetting your profile, reaching Prestige, or creating a Seasonal character;
- Increased the price of Ragman's basic Tactical Clothing;
- The Predator Upper and Adik Tracksuit, unlocked through achievements, no longer require purchase and are permanently unlocked on your account immediately.

- After your PMC dies, you can now spectate any surviving squadmate until they die or the raid ends;
- You can leave spectator mode at any time and proceed to the raid end screen;
- Spectator mode now activates automatically after your PMC dies. This can be disabled in the game settings.

- Support messages now more accurately identify players who have fallen into difficult situations;
- Players who die in a raid while in severe financial and equipment hardship will now receive a support message containing a special container with enough gear for a fully equipped raid;
- This support package can be received no more than once every 18 hours, and the message must also be claimed within 18 hours of being received.

Added one-way progression synchronization from EFT: Arena to PvP Season.

The following progress is transferred from EFT: Arena to PvP Season:
- PMC experience earned;
- Skill and weapon mastery experience;
- Trader reputation and unlocked trade offers;
- Currency, GP Coins, Lega Medals, and gear crates after completing the Jack of All Trades task in EFT: Arena;
- Unlocked Tactical Clothing.

The transfer limit for currency and items in PvP Season has been reduced compared to PvP Zone.

Tactical Clothing is synchronized between EFT: Arena and PvP Season in both directions. If Tactical Clothing is unlocked in one game, it automatically becomes available in the other.

Important! Only PMC experience and trader reputation earned in EFT: Arena after the start of the KORD BREACH season will be transferred to PvP Season.
- Previously earned progress will not be transferred.
- Item transfers and Seasonal character progression sync from PvP Season to EFT: Arena are not supported.
- For example, if your EFT: Arena character had already reached Level 78 before the season began, that level will not be transferred to PvP Season. However, if you earn, for example, 10,000 PMC experience in EFT: Arena after the start of the season, that experience will also be awarded to your Seasonal character.

The player profile now displays:
- Selected Personal modifiers;
- KORD BREACH Battle Pass progress.

Added new interactive mechanics across locations:
- Padlocks on certain doors;
- Padlocks on certain containers;
- Openable elevator doors.

Added new interactive environmental effects:
- Breakable bottles;
- Exploding fire extinguishers;
- Vehicles that emit smoke after being hit.

Exploding gas cylinders have also been added to additional locations. Their visual explosion effects have been reworked.

- Norinco QBZ-191 5.8x42 assault rifle;
- Howa Type 20 5.56x45 assault rifle;
- HK 416A5 5.56x45 assault rifle in RAL 8000 color;
- New attachments for PKM/PKP, AKS074U, FN SCAR, AR-15, and more;
- New 5.8x42mm caliber:
  - DBP191 general-purpose cartridge;
  - DBX95 tracer cartridge;
  - DVC12 armor-piercing cartridge;
  - DBX12 armor-piercing tracer cartridge.
- 4 new streamer items;
- 2 new Tactical Clothing sets:
  - USEC Corsair;
  - BEAR Airborne Infantry.

- Fixed an incorrect third-person player animation when stopping after walking;
- Fixed the missing weapon sway while aiming;
- Fixed the missing reload animations for bots in certain cases;
- Fixed multiple culling issues across locations;
- Fixed several incorrect voice lines for the USEC Rob voice;
- Fixed the incorrect trader reputation calculations after reaching Prestige;
- Fixed the incorrect distant LOD of the Lantac Dragon 5.56x45 muzzle brake;
- Fixed the ricochet settings for gear with armor points, including armor vests, plate carriers, helmets, additional armor components, and more;
- Fixed a UI freeze that could occur while interacting with the BTR Driver dialogue in certain cases;
- Fixed the issue with the skill leveling bonus from trophies in the Hall of Fame, and removed the requirement for the player to personally score the kill;
- Fixed an error that could occur when loading into a raid in certain cases.

Balancing changes for the "Blackout" event:
- Raid duration on The Lab has been increased to 30 minutes in PvP and 35 minutes in PvE;
- In PvE, the number of Black Division operatives has been reduced, and the number of PMC bots has been increased on The Lab;
- Increased the chance for Black Division operatives to spawn with the arsenal storage room key;
- Any target now counts toward the progress of the "If I Can't Have It" task;
- Increased the amount of loot in locked rooms on The Lab;
- Added new TerraGroup Labs access keycard offers to Therapist and Mechanic.

Fixes:
- Fixed the missing voice announcement during power outage on The Lab in PvE;
- Fixed incorrect UI display after opening the "Map" tab on the location selection screen.

- Fixed an issue that caused weapons to overheat too quickly on Streets of Tarkov in certain cases;
- Fixed an issue where weapons could remain suspended in midair after a player's death in certain cases;
- Fixed the incorrect female voice audio in The Lab;
- Fixed the incorrect audio for certain gunshots at medium range;
- Fixed a number of incorrect UI elements on the Character and Weapon Builds screens;
- Fixed an incorrect animation for the MSGL grenade launcher's cylinder in certain cases.

- Increased the time it takes for Rogues to spot an enemy;
- Black Division will now spread out more evenly when moving towards players before spotting them in the engine room;
- The Wedge boss will now deploy more gas grenade tripwires;
- Black Division will now use grenades more frequently in the engine room and on the helipad;
- Fixed an issue where Knight boss could enter the deck through a door;
- Fixed an issue where Black Division would not move towards the player in the engine room and would remain stationary.

- Fixed a missing QTE progress indicator in the Gym module in Hideout;
- Several geometry changes were made to the Icebreaker location;
- Fixed a problem that could cause PMC softlock after reloading weapons.

- Decreased reaction speed for the boss Wedge and his guards;
- Increased bot detection speed on the Icebreaker;
- Added flashbang and gas grenades to the Black Division bot arsenal;
- Added additional Rogue spawn points on Icebreaker.

- Added a mechanic that assists players in locating in-raid items required for tasks. Players will now see an expanded directional indicator when approaching the spawn location of a required task item;
- Added additional notifications when interacting with signal flare extractions;
- Added an experimental graphics setting that shifts the load of certain light sources from the CPU to the GPU. The option is available for higher-end graphics cards;
- Increased chance of death after injecting Obdolbos 1 to 33%;
- Added several new streamer items.

- Fixed a cause of memory leaks related to the audio system in certain cases;
- Optimized the animation system to reduce CPU usage;
- Fixed an issue where the limb selection interface for healing could disappear in certain situations;
- Fixed visual artifacts when using x2 and x4 resampling while interacting with Traders and the Hideout in certain cases;
- Fixed the cause of error 228 that could occur when removing an expiring water filter from the Water Collector zone in the Hideout;
- Fixed several visual issues related to geometry and colliders across locations;
- Fixed a cause of severe client performance drops when dragging ammo from the inventory over a full magazine in the search window;
- Fixed an issue where kills with Saiga-12K 12ga automatic shotgun (Redline) did not count towards progression of the tasks "Silent Caliber" and "Punisher p.4";
- Fixed the incorrect compass behavior after exiting the BTR;
- Number of minor fixes to various aspects of the game.

- Improvements aimed at optimizing off-raid screens;
- Increased the FPS limit in menus and added an option to adjust it in the game settings;
- Several changes to the animation system and audio engine to improve PC resource usage;
- Reworked the architecture of post-raid systems to further reduce the time required to exit a raid and return to the menu;
- As part of optimization efforts, an updated player culling system has been implemented on Lighthouse, Shoreline, Woods, and Ground Zero. The system will be introduced to the remaining locations in future updates;
- Implemented an iteration of environment object and geometry optimization for Streets of Tarkov to improve location performance;
- Please note that the impact of these changes will depend on your PC configuration and in-game settings.
- Introduced a task progression protection system in local PvE Zone raids in case of unexpected client shutdowns. If the game closes unexpectedly, task progress will now revert to the state at the start of the raid;
- Updated the left-shoulder firing stance logic. Switching to the right shoulder will no longer happen instantly when colliding with obstacles. Instead, the weapon will continue moving for a short period without changing stance;
- Updated the K/D display in character stats. It now counts player kills only.

With this update, we introduce the second stage of weapon mod adjustments, focusing on barrels and handguards. Muzzle devices and stocks were further adjusted based on the first iteration.

Barrels follow the same principle as before. Longer barrels provide greater recoil reduction but impose higher ergonomics penalties. Changes were made to:
- Standardize parameters and make them clearer.
- Make the choice between short and long barrels more meaningful.

Handguards no longer reduce recoil. Their role is now to offset ergonomics penalties imposed by barrels.

Muzzle devices were further refined following the first iteration. Suppressors and their combinations with compensators now reduce ergonomics more and affect recoil less.

These changes are intended to further increase the popularity of unsuppressed weapon builds. Adjustments to muzzle flash are planned for future updates.

Buttstocks received minor adjustments, mainly addressing inaccuracies and issues from the first iteration.

Base characteristics of many weapons have been updated to better align with the new balance. Recoil and ergonomics have been improved for the following:
- All AK, AKM, and AK-100 series weapons;
- Steyr AUG A1;
- Steyr AUG A3;
- HK G36;
- HK 416A5;
- FN SCAR-L;
- FN SCAR-H;
- SIG MCX-SPEAR;
- SIG MCX .300;
- CMMG Mk47 Mutant;
- Rifle Dynamics RD-704;
- Aklys Defense Velociraptor;
- All machine guns;
- All bolt-action and marksman rifles chambered in 7.62x51, 7.62x54R, .338, and .50 BMG.

- Fixed an issue where dead players and bots could appear to move visually in certain cases;
- Fixed an issue where damage would not register after a weapon malfunction if the player had previously used a stationary weapon;
- Fixed the cause of error 228 during trader dialogues that could block task progression;
- Fixes to culling, shadows, textures, and location geometry;
- Fixed an issue where armor could not be picked up if it was dropped while interacting with the modification window;
- Fixed the incorrect behavior of PMC bots toward player Scavs with Fence reputation 6 or higher in PvE Zone;
- Fixed an issue preventing further progression in The Labyrinth after spawning in the room requiring a burner tool to exit;
- Fixed the incorrect display of smoke grenades in the player’s hands if another player threw a smoke grenade at them;
- Fixed the display of changes in the "Combat Skill Leveling Boost" field in the Hall of Fame Hideout zone when one dogtag was replaced with another of a similar level;
- Fixed an issue where PostFX settings would not display when preview was enabled;
- Fixed an issue where some players could get stuck in the secret saferoom on Interchange without a way to exit;
- Fixed the incorrect display of stationary weapons used by bots and multiple cases where bots could float while using them;
- Fixed multiple issues with incorrect behavior of loot and gear items when dropped in raid;
- Fixed the display of current movement noise level and stance height during raids;
- Fixed the third-person animation for inspecting your own inventory.

- Fixed an issue where Kerman would not send the Secure container Alpha-1 with TerraGroup evidence after the player died at the Terminal;
- Fixed an issue where items could not be handed over as part of tasks in local raids in the PvE Zone if they were in the player’s backpack;
- Fixed an issue with completing Fence's operational tasks to find items in local raids in the PvE Zone;
- Fixed the display of crafting progress in the Hideout module icons.

- Fixed incorrect display of PMC hands in first and third person when using the MP7A2;
- Fixed an issue preventing the player from using the paid exit;
- Fixed incorrect camera behavior when adjusting the camera's alignment while using the GP-25 "Bonfire".

- Multiple improvements aimed at optimizing client performance across all locations. The impact of these changes will depend on the player’s hardware configuration and in-game settings;
- As part of optimization efforts, an updated player culling system has been implemented on Customs, Interchange, and Reserve. This system has already been active on Streets of Tarkov. Implementation on all locations is planned in future updates;
- Improved the responsiveness and smoothness of main menu tabs and dialogue loading;
- Added the ability to play as a Scav solo in PvE Zone on a local client to reduce raid matchmaking time;
- Added further improvements aimed at reducing online raid loading times;
- Adjusted the healing priority for multifunctional medkits: after treating bleedings, priority is now given to head and thorax;
- Added magazine drop sounds during reload and when discarding magazines.

- Figurines and posters previously available as rewards during the Release Twitch Drops event now spawn on locations;
- Increased the available time window for transitioning from Shoreline to Terminal;
- Increased the experience gained for completing PMC operational tasks;
- Significantly simplified the PMC operational task objectives;
- Removed the objectives for co-op extraction in both PMC and Scav operational tasks;
- Reduced the number of Priest kills required for completion in the story chapter "They Are Already Here" to 1;
- Reduced the trader response wait timers by 40% in the following story chapters: Falling Skies, The Ticket, The Unheard, The Labyrinth, and Batya;
- Added alternative objectives to the story chapter "Tour" to simplify location unlocks. Players can now either visit the location multiple times or survive on it one time to complete the objective;
- Reduced the duration of most Hideout crafts required for story progression by 40%;
- Standardized the protection zones of front and rear built-in armor for light armor vests and armored rigs;
- Adjusted the prices for most armor vests and armored rigs. Prices of plate carriers without built-in armor have been significantly reduced;
- Increased the Raider count in The Lab by 20%;
- Increased the quantity and quality of loot in locked and marked rooms;
- Increased the fuel tank spawn chance at gas stations on Customs, Lighthouse, and Shoreline;
- Reduced the arming distance of the 40mm VOG-25 round to 10 meters;
- Reduced the trader sell price of the 40x46mm M386 (HE) grenade;
- Increased the trader sell price of the 40mm VOG-25 grenade.

Expanded the objective areas for elimination tasks with specific zones:
