Flash hiders, muzzle brakes, and similar attachments now reduce recoil more effectively;

Suppressors, including their combos with various muzzle brakes, now have a smaller impact on recoil. In exchange, their ergonomics penalty has been reduced.

These changes are aimed at addressing the current prevalence of suppressors, which are used almost universally. We want players to make a choice when building weapons: better recoil control with a muzzle brake versus relative stealth with a suppressor.

